    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": ": Pt here for follow-up on atrial fibrillation / flutter. Atrial fibrillation / flutter (normal echo; CHA2DS2-VASc 1; onset 4.2 years ago) - controlled. Dental abscess - controlled. Urinary tract infection - controlled. BP 150/90. Wt 172 lbs. Cardiac exam shows no new abnormalities. Patient reports compliance with prescribed medications. Continues regular exercise and tobacco use (cigar) at a frequency of 12 times per year.\n\n---\n\n**Assessment and Plan:**\n\nMs. Amanda Kelley is a 61-year-old female who has been under my care since 2020 for multiple chronic conditions. She presents today for follow-up on her vitamin D deficiency, with a history of atrial fibrillation/flutter, abscess, urinary tract infection, and eczema.\n\n**Atrial fibrillation/flutter (normal echo; CHA2DS2-VASc 1; 4.2 years ago):**\n- Ms. Kelley has been stable with controlled atrial fibrillation/flutter for the past 4.2 years. The remains normal, and the CHA2DS2-VASc score is 1, indicating a low risk of stroke. She has no history of ablation procedures. She continues to be compliant with her medication regimen, and there have been no recent episodes of arrhythmia.\n\n**Dental abscess:**\n- The dental abscess resolved successfully following treatment with amoxicillin 875 mg and hydrocodone-acetaminophen 5/325 mg. The patient has been symptom-free for over a decade.\n\n**Urinary tract infection:**\n- Ms. Kelley’s history of urinary tract infections has been well-managed with appropriate antibiotic therapy, including sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim 800/160 mg and nitrofurantoin 100 mg. She has had no recurrence of UTIs for several years.\n\n**Vitamin D deficiency:**\n- Ms. Kelley has been receiving ergocalciferol 50000 IU to manage her vitamin D deficiency. Her recent lab results indicate adequate vitamin D levels, and she reports no related symptoms.\n\n**Eczema:**\n- The eczema has been well-controlled with tacrolimus topical 0.1%. The patient reports minimal flare-ups and has been compliant with her topical treatment regimen.\n\n**History of syncope:**\n- There has been no recurrence syncope episodes since her last evaluation. She remains under regular follow-up to monitor for any potential recurrence.\n\n**Elevated function tests (resolved):**\n- Previous elevated liver function tests have resolved with appropriate management and monitoring.\n\n**Social History:**\n- Ms. Kelley exercises regularly, running 3-4 times a week. She currently uses tobacco in the form of cigars at a frequency of 12 times per year. She has been honest about her tobacco use.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMs. Kelle"
